<title>AUSTRALIA: St George Bank half year net profit jumps.</title>
<headline>St George Bank half year net profit jumps.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   166.61 vs 121.15</p>
<p>    Net				     99.74 vs 74.52</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		    26    vs 26</p>
<p>NOTE: St George Bank Ltd recently merged with Advance Bank. These are the first combined results.  </p>
<p>    Interest income		  1,095.93 vs 850.53</p>
<p>    Interest expense		   690.29 vs 551.98</p>
<p>    Other income			  91.33 vs 61.32</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    58.4 vs 73.9</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			  nil vs loss 1.2</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date July 2</p>
<p>Reg date June 13</p>
<p>    Tax				     66.47 vs 45.13</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  45.22 vs 22.29</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.41 vs 0.29</p>
<p>    Total assets (billion)	    41.98 vs 18.76</p>
<p>NOTE: Advance Bank contribution from January 30 to March 31.</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    38.5</p>
<p>    Net profit			    19.1</p>
<p>    Interest income		    266.9</p>
<p>    Interest expense		   172.8</p>
<p>    Other income			  27.3</p>
<p>    Tax				     19.4</p>
<p>--Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
